T1  - Cost-effectiveness ofstructured medication review for heart failure with
preserved ejection fraction: a pragmatic registry analysis
JF  - Journal of Clinical Epidemiology
PY  - 2025
U3  - Journal Article
Clinical Trial
AB  - A within-trial economic evaluation estimated healthcare use and costs
associated with structured medication review for heart failure with preserved
ejection fraction. Resource use, service contacts, medication changes, and
quality-adjusted survival were compared with standard care. Results were
sensitive to assumptions about intervention delivery and longer-term
maintenance. The economic model varied staff time, service intensity, and the
assumed duration of treatment benefit. The authors described uncertainty around
maintenance of the observed pattern beyond follow-up.
