T1  - Clinical outcomes after pharmacist-led medication review for hypertension: a report on clinical decision-making
JF  - BMJ Open
PY  - 2025
U3  - Journal Article
Clinical Trial
AB  - Investigators explored pharmacist-led medication review against standard care in 435 adults with hypertension. The intervention showed a small but measurable benefit for blood pressure control, while treatment exposure and adverse events were broadly comparable between groups. Generalisability may be reduced because participating sites had established research infrastructure. Results were interpreted alongside baseline severity, treatment exposure, and concurrent care.
