AB  - A prespecified secondary analysis examined variation in depressive symptom severity after guided behavioural activation among adults with major depressive disorder. Effects were explored by baseline severity, age, adherence, and recruitment setting. The pattern was directionally consistent with the primary analysis, but subgroup estimates were imprecise. The report discusses how missing observations may affect interpretation of the final estimates.
